course: dictionary
lesson: 3715
title: Flexibility: bending and changing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Flexibility is a noun with two main meanings. The first is the ability to bend easily without breaking, like a stretchy ruler or your own body when you stretch. The second is the ability to change or fit in with new situations or plans, like a flexible bedtime or a flexible timetable.
explain: «Muscles stretch further and more safely when warm; forcing a stretch into sharp pain can tear a muscle, and flexibility grows slowly over weeks.» The clues are warm, safely, tear and slowly. Here flexibility means how far your body can bend and stretch, and it grows slowly, not all at once.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "Flexibility grows slowly over weeks" makes sense if flexibility means how far you can bend. It would not make sense if it meant the colour of your socks. So the meaning fits the context.
fact: Flexibility means the ability to bend easily without breaking.
fact: Flexibility can also mean being able to change or fit in with new situations or plans.
fact: Flexibility is an uncountable noun, so we say more flexibility, not "a flexibility" or "two flexibilities".
fact: Useful phrases are show flexibility and improve flexibility.
fact: Rubber has flexibility, so it can bend and stretch in science.
exercise: In «Muscles stretch further when warm», what does flexibility mean? | How loud your voice is | The colour of a muscle | *How far a muscle can bend and stretch | How many muscles you have
exercise: A club says its meeting times are flexible. What does flexible mean here? | Bendy like a ruler | Very loud | *Able to change to fit in with new plans | Always the same
exercise: Which is correct? | a flexibility | more flexibility | two flexibilities | *more flexibility, not flexibilities
test: «Rubber is useful because it has flexibility.» What does this mean? | Rubber is always hard | Rubber is always wet | Rubber is very heavy | *Rubber can bend and stretch without breaking
test: Sam says, "I can show flexibility if the match is moved." What does Sam mean? | He will not play at all | He is afraid of the match | He is very bendy like a gymnast | *He can change his plans to fit the new time
exam: Which sentence uses flexibility in the sense of changing plans? | I can see flexibility in the sky | We ate flexibility for lunch | *Our club can move the meeting to Friday, showing flexibility | The stone wall has flexibility
